ses":["cost","stats"],"builtin":true},{"name":"insights","description":"Generate a report analyzing your Claude Code sessions","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"recap","description":"Generate a one-line session recap now","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"goal","description":"Set a goal — keep working until the condition is met","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"list-agents","description":"List subagents, teammates, and other Claude sessions you can message","argumentHint":"","aliases":["peers"],"builtin":true},{"name":"team-onboarding","description":"Help teammates ramp on Claude Code with a guide from your usage","argumentHint":"","builtin":true}],"uuid":"050ff1de-8ad9-4e33-b745-7322ac53579b","session_id":"163efe90-675b-4e09-a080-713d4bfbbf15"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KzupdqPp91H3LmNArP7WpZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Candidate conformal prediction-set procedure for compositional (softmax) outputs.\n2\t\n3\tEntry point: ``handle(request) -> response`` (``python_rpc_v1:handle``).  The wire protocol is\n4\tidentical to the starter (reset / calibrate / predict; responses ``{\"ok\": true}`` and\n5\t``{\"sets\": MASK}``); see the starter docstring for the message layout.  No diagnostic fields are\n6\tadded to any response.\n7\t\n8\tMethod (simplex-geometry aware split conformal with Mondrian calibration):\n9\t\n10\t* Score: LAC score ``1 - p[label]`` (an Aitchison-vertex score is available as an alternative\n11\t  through ``_SCORE`` but the LAC score gave the smallest sets in design, see notes in memory).\n12\t* K <= 10: the evaluator's slices are classes, so we use class-conditional (Mondrian by label)\n13\t  thresholds, shrunk toward the pooled threshold for classes with few calibration rows.\n14\t* K > 10: Mondrian by predicted-confidence bin (max probability), a taxon that depends on x only\n15\t  so the guarantee is exact conditional on the bin.\n16\t* Finite-sample quantile level ``ceil((n + 1)(1 - alpha)) / n`` with a small variance-aware\n17\t  inflation: the expected under-coverage penalty is far steeper than the size cost of a tiny\n18\t  extra margin, and the margin scales with the Beta(n + 1 - l, l) coverage standard deviation.\n19\t\n20\tGated domain-classifier weighting (this candidate's addition): the unlabeled test probabilities\n21\tseen so far are compared with the calibration probabilities through a cross-fitted, ridge-penalised\n22\tlogistic domain classifier on a few sorted-probability summary features.  The held-out\n23\tlikelihood-ratio statistic LR gives a positive-part shrinkage beta = max(0, 1 - d / LR); when\n24\tbeta is (numerically) zero -- always the case under exchangeability, where the held-out LR is\n25\tnon-positive -- the unweighted Mondrian thresholds above are used verbatim (exact no-op).  Otherwise\n26\tper-test-row weighted Mondrian thresholds (Tibshirani et al. 2019, test mass at +inf) are used,\n27\twith effective-sample-size margins; any non-finite quantity falls back to the unweighted path.\n28\t\n29\tThe remaining helpers (CLR/ILR transforms, Aitchison distance, ILR volume, worst-slab coverage,\n30\tweighted conformal quantile, Beta coverage law, paired sign-flip test, Holm correction) implement\n31\tthe evaluation protocol of the research idea; they are only used internally.\n32\t\"\"\"\n33\timport base64\n34\timport math\n35\t\n36\timport numpy as np\n37\t\n38\ttry:  # scipy is optional for the serving path\n39\t    import scipy.stats\n40\texcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover\n41\t    scipy = None\n42\t\n43\t_state = {}\n44\t\n45\t_SCORE = \"lac\"          # \"lac\" or \"aitchison\"\n46\t_EPS = 1e-6             # simplex floor for log-ratio transforms\n47\t_Z_GLOBAL = 0.7         # margin multipliers (in coverage standard deviations)\n48\t_Z_GROUP = 0.6\n49\t_SHRINK_N0 = 20.0       # pseudo-count for shrinking group thresholds toward the pooled one\n50\t_MIN_BIN = 80           # minimal calibration rows per confidence bin\n51\t_MAX_BINS = 10\n52\t_MAX_CLASSCOND_K = 10\n53\t_RIDGE = 1.0            # ridge penalty of the domain classifier (standardised features)\n54\t_MIN_TEST_DOMAIN = 40   # minimal unlabeled test rows before the domain classifier is fitted\n55\t_BETA_ON = 1e-3         # weights are used only if the shrinkage factor exceeds this\n56\t_W_CLIP = 8.0           # weights clipped to [1/_W_CLIP, _W_CLIP]\n57\t_FEAT_CLIP = 8.0        # standardised features clipped to +-_FEAT_CLIP\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- wire helpers\n61\tdef _decode(obj):\n62\t    dtype = np.dtype(obj[\"dtype\"]).newbyteorder(\"<\")\n63\t    arr = np.frombuffer(base64.b64decode(obj[\"data\"]), dtype=dtype)\n64\t    return arr.reshape(obj[\"shape\"])\n65\t\n66\t\n67\tdef _encode_mask(mask):\n68\t    packed = np.packbits(mask.astype(np.uint8), axis=1)\n69\t    return {\"dtype\": \"uint8\", \"shape\": [int(mask.shape[0]), int(mask.shape[1])],\n70\t            \"encoding\": \"packbits_base64\", \"data\": base64.b64encode(packed.tobytes()).decode(\"ascii\")}\n71\t\n72\t\n73\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- compositional geometry\n74\tdef _close(p, eps=_EPS):\n75\t    p = np.clip(np.asarray(p, dtype=np.float64), eps, None)\n76\t    return p / p.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n77\t\n78\t\n79\tdef clr_transform(p, eps=_EPS):\n80\t    \"\"\"Centred log-ratio transform of compositions along the last axis (with simplex floor).\"\"\"\n81\t    lp = np.log(_close(p, eps))\n82\t    return lp - lp.mean(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n83\t\n84\t\n85\tdef _helmert_basis(D):\n86\t    \"\"\"Orthonormal basis (D x (D-1)) of the CLR hyperplane (Helmert contrast matrix).\"\"\"\n87\t    V = np.zeros((D, D - 1))\n88\t    for j in range(1, D):\n89\t        V[:j, j - 1] = 1.0 / j\n90\t        V[j, j - 1] = -1.0\n91\t        V[:, j - 1] *= math.sqrt(j / (j + 1.0))\n92\t    return V\n93\t\n94\t\n95\tdef ilr_transform(p, eps=_EPS):\n96\t    \"\"\"Isometric log-ratio coordinates in R^(D-1) (Egozcue et al. style Helmert basis).\"\"\"\n97\t    c = clr_transform(p, eps)\n98\t    return c @ _helmert_basis(c.shape[-1])\n99\t\n100\t\n101\tdef aitchison_distance(a, b, eps=_EPS):\n102\t    \"\"\"Aitchison distance = Euclidean distance between CLR (equivalently ILR) coordinates.\"\"\"\n103\t    return np.linalg.norm(clr_transform(a, eps) - clr_transform(b, eps), axis=-1)\n104\t\n105\t\n106\tdef ilr_log_volume(radius, D):\n107\t    \"\"\"Log-volume of a (D-1)-dimensional ILR-space ball: (D-1) log r + log V_{D-1}(1).\"\"\"\n108\t    d = D - 1\n109\t    return d * np.log(np.maximum(radius, 1e-300)) + (d / 2.0) * math.log(math.pi) - math.lgamma(d / 2.0 + 1.0)\n110\t\n111\t\n112\tdef _score_matrix(probs):\n113\t    \"\"\"Nonconformity score of every candidate label, shape [n, K].\"\"\"\n114\t    if _SCORE == \"aitchison\":\n115\t        K = probs.shape[1]\n116\t        c = clr_transform(probs)\n117\t        lo, hi = math.log(_EPS), math.log(1.0)\n118\t        # smoothed vertex e_j has clr = log(v) - mean(log v)\n119\t        v = np.full(K, _EPS)\n120\t        out = np.empty_like(probs, dtype=np.float64)\n121\t        for j in range(K):\n122\t            vj = v.copy()\n123\t            vj[j] = 1.0\n124\t            vj = vj / vj.sum()\n125\t            cj = np.log(vj) - np.log(vj).mean()\n126\t            out[:, j] = np.linalg.norm(c - cj, axis=1)\n127\t        return out\n128\t    return 1.0 - probs\n129\t\n130\t\n131\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- conformal quantiles\n132\tdef finite_sample_level(n, alpha):\n133\t    \"\"\"Conformal quantile level ceil((n + 1)(1 - alpha)) / n (may exceed 1 for tiny n).\"\"\"\n134\t    alpha = float(alpha) + 1e-12  # guards float round-off in (n + 1) * (1 - alpha)\n135\t    return np.ceil((n + 1) * (1 - alpha)) / n\n136\t\n137\t\n138\tdef _kth_smallest(scores, level):\n139\t    n = len(scores)\n140\t    if n == 0 or level > 1.0:\n141\t        return math.inf\n142\t    k = int(np.rint(level * n))\n143\t    return float(np.sort(scores)[min(max(k, 1), n) - 1])\n144\t\n145\t\n146\tdef _quantile(scores, alpha):\n147\t    scores = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float64)\n148\t    return _kth_smallest(scores, finite_sample_level(len(scores), alpha))\n149\t\n150\t\n151\tdef weighted_conformal_quantile(scores, weights, test_weight, alpha):\n152\t    \"\"\"Likelihood-ratio weighted conformal quantile (Tibshirani et al. 2019).\n153\t\n154\t    Calibration points carry weights w(x_i); the test point's mass w(x) sits at +inf.\n155\t    \"\"\"\n156\t    scores = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float64)\n157\t    weights = np.asarray(weights, dtype=np.float64)\n158\t    order = np.argsort(scores)\n159\t    s, w = scores[order], weights[order]\n160\t    p = w / (w.sum() + test_weight)\n161\t    cum = np.cumsum(p)\n162\t    idx = np.searchsorted(cum, 1.0 - alpha - 1e-12, side=\"left\")\n163\t    return math.inf if idx >= len(s) else float(s[idx])\n164\t\n165\t\n166\tdef beta_coverage_law(n, alpha):\n167\t    \"\"\"Frozen Beta(n + 1 - l, l) law of split-conformal coverage, l = floor((n + 1) alpha).\"\"\"\n168\t    l = int(math.floor((n + 1) * alpha + 1e-12))\n169\t    l = max(l, 1)\n170\t    if scipy is not None:\n171\t        return scipy.stats.beta(n + 1 - l, l)\n172\t    return None\n173\t\n174\t\n175\tdef mondrian_conformal_quantile(scores, groups, n_groups, alpha, n_total_test=None,\n176\t                                z_group=_Z_GROUP, z_global=_Z_GLOBAL, n0=_SHRINK_N0):\n177\t    \"\"\"Per-group conformal thresholds (Mondrian calibration) with pooled-threshold shrinkage.\n178\t\n179\t    ``scores`` are calibration scores, ``groups`` integer taxon ids in [0, n_groups).  Returns an\n180\t    array ``q`` of length ``n_groups``.  Each group's level is the finite-sample level\n181\t    ceil((n_g + 1)(1 - alpha_g))/n_g with alpha_g reduced by ``z_group`` coverage standard\n182\t    deviations; groups too small to support a finite quantile fall back to the pooled threshold.\n183\t    \"\"\"\n184\t    scores = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float64)\n185\t    groups = np.asarray(groups)\n186\t    N = len(scores)\n187\t    a = float(alpha)\n188\t    var = a * (1.0 - a)\n189\t    inv_m = 0.0 if not n_total_test else 1.0 / float(n_total_test)\n190\t    a_glob = max(a - z_global * math.sqrt(var * (1.0 / max(N, 1) + inv_m)), 1e-6)\n191\t    q_glob = _quantile(scores, a_glob)\n192\t    if not np.isfinite(q_glob):\n193\t        q_glob = _quantile(scores, a)\n194\t    q = np.full(n_groups, q_glob)\n195\t    for g in range(n_groups):\n196\t        sg = scores[groups == g]\n197\t        ng = len(sg)\n198\t        if ng == 0 or not np.isfinite(_quantile(sg, a)):\n199\t            continue\n200\t        k_g = float(n_groups) * inv_m if n_total_test else 0.0\n201\t        a_g = max(a - z_group * math.sqrt(var * (1.0 / ng + k_g)), 1e-6)\n202\t        qg = _kth_smallest(sg, min(1.0, finite_sample_level(ng, a_g)))\n203\t        lam = ng / (ng + n0)\n204\t        q[g] = lam * qg + (1.0 - lam) * q_glob\n205\t    return q\n206\t\n207\t\n208\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- evaluation helpers\n209\tdef worst_slab_coverage(covered, slab_ids):\n210\t    \"\"\"Minimum empirical coverage over slabs and the worst-slab gap to the best slab-free mean.\"\"\"\n211\t    covered = np.asarray(covered, dtype=np.float64)\n212\t    slab_ids = np.asarray(slab_ids)\n213\t    covs = [covered[slab_ids == s].mean() for s in np.unique(slab_ids)]\n214\t    return float(min(covs)) if covs else float(\"nan\")\n215\t\n216\t\n217\tdef paired_sign_flip_test(diffs, n_perm=2000, seed=0):\n218\t    \"\"\"Two-sided paired sign-flip permutation test on per-draw differences between methods.\"\"\"\n219\t    diffs = np.asarray(diffs, dtype=np.float64)\n220\t    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n221\t    obs = abs(diffs.mean())\n222\t    signs = rng.choice([-1.0, 1.0], size=(n_perm, len(diffs)))\n223\t    perm = np.abs((signs * diffs).mean(axis=1))\n224\t    return float((1 + np.sum(perm >= obs - 1e-15)) / (n_perm + 1))\n225\t\n226\t\n227\tdef holm_correction(pvals):\n228\t    \"\"\"Holm-Bonferroni step-down adjusted p-values.\"\"\"\n229\t    p = np.asarray(pvals, dtype=np.float64)\n230\t    m = len(p)\n231\t    order = np.argsort(p)\n232\t    adj = np.empty(m)\n233\t    running = 0.0\n234\t    for rank, i in enumerate(order):\n235\t        running = max(running, (m - rank) * p[i])\n236\t        adj[i] = min(1.0, running)\n237\t    return adj\n238\t\n239\t\n240\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- serving path\n241\tdef _bin_edges(maxp, n_bins):\n242\t    if n_bins <= 1:\n243\t        return np.zeros(0)\n244\t    return np.quantile(maxp, np.arange(1, n_bins) / n_bins)\n245\t\n246\t\n247\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- domain-classifier weights\n248\tdef _summary_features(probs):\n249\t    \"\"\"Low-dimensional sorted-probability summary of each row, shape [n, 5].\n250\t\n251\t    [logit(max prob), top1-top2 log ratio, normalised entropy, mean top-5 log prob minus top-1\n252\t    log prob, log of the normalised Gini impurity]; all from probabilities clipped at 1e-6.\n253\t    \"\"\"\n254\t    p = np.clip(np.asarray(probs, dtype=np.float64), _EPS, 1.0)\n255\t    K = p.shape[1]\n256\t    ps = -np.sort(-p, axis=1)\n257\t    ls = np.log(ps)\n258\t    k5 = min(K, 5)\n259\t    pmax = ps[:, 0]\n260\t    f1 = np.log(pmax) - np.log(np.maximum(1.0 - pmax, _EPS))\n261\t    f2 = ls[:, 0] - ls[:, 1] if K > 1 else np.zeros(len(p))\n262\t    f3 = -(p * np.log(p)).sum(axis=1) / max(math.log(K), 1e-12)\n263\t    f4 = ls[:, :k5].mean(axis=1) - ls[:, 0]\n264\t    gini = (1.0 - (p * p).sum(axis=1)) / max(1.0 - 1.0 / K, 1e-12)\n265\t    f5 = np.log(np.clip(gini, _EPS, None))\n266\t    return np.stack([f1, f2, f3, f4, f5], axis=1)\n267\t\n268\t\n269\tdef _fit_domain_logistic(X, y, sw, ridge=_RIDGE, iters=25):\n270\t    \"\"\"Ridge-penalised weighted logistic regression by IRLS (Newton); returns [coef..., intercept].\"\"\"\n271\t    n, d = X.shape\n272\t    A = np.concatenate([X, np.ones((n, 1))], axis=1)\n273\t    R = ridge * np.eye(d + 1)\n274\t    R[d, d] = 1e-8\n275\t    b = np.zeros(d + 1)\n276\t    for _ in range(iters):\n277\t        eta = np.clip(A @ b, -30.0, 30.0)\n278\t        p = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-eta))\n279\t        g = A.T @ (sw * (p - y)) + R @ b\n280\t        H = (A * (sw * p * (1.0 - p))[:, None]).T @ A + R\n281\t        step = np.linalg.solve(H, g)\n282\t        step = np.clip(step, -5.0, 5.0)\n283\t        b = b - step\n284\t        if np.max(np.abs(step)) < 1e-7:\n285\t            break\n286\t    return b\n287\t\n288\t\n289\tdef _positive_part_shrink(lr, df):\n290\t    \"\"\"James-Stein style positive-part shrinkage factor beta = max(0, 1 - df / LR).\"\"\"\n291\t    if not np.isfinite(lr) or lr <= 0.0:\n292\t        return 0.0\n293\t    return max(0.0, 1.0 - df / lr)\n294\t\n295\t\n296\tdef _domain_logweights(Fc, Ft, fold_c):\n297\t    \"\"\"Cross-fitted domain-classifier log density ratios (test over calibration).\n298\t\n299\t    Returns (beta, z_cal, z_test): ``beta`` the positive-part shrinkage factor computed from the\n300\t    held-out likelihood-ratio statistic, ``z`` the centred held-out log-odds (balanced classes).\n301\t    A row's value always comes from a model fitted on the other fold (2-fold cross-fitting over\n302\t    calibration rows and over test rows).\n303\t    \"\"\"\n304\t    nc, d = Fc.shape\n305\t    nt = Ft.shape[0]\n306\t    fold_t = np.arange(nt) % 2\n307\t    zc = np.zeros(nc)\n308\t    zt = np.zeros(nt)\n309\t    ll_full = 0.0\n310\t    ll_null = 0.0\n311\t    for f in (0, 1):\n312\t        trc, tec = fold_c != f, fold_c == f\n313\t        trt, tet = fold_t != f, fold_t == f\n314\t        ncr, ntr = int(trc.sum()), int(trt.sum())\n315\t        if ncr < 5 or ntr < 5 or tec.sum() < 1 or tet.sum() < 1:\n316\t            return 0.0, zc, zt\n317\t        X = np.concatenate([Fc[trc], Ft[trt]], axis=0)\n318\t        y = np.concatenate([np.zeros(ncr), np.ones(ntr)])\n319\t        n = ncr + ntr\n320\t        sw = np.where(y > 0.5, n / (2.0 * ntr), n / (2.0 * ncr))\n321\t        b = _fit_domain_logistic(X, y, sw)\n322\t        ec = Fc[tec] @ b[:-1] + b[-1]\n323\t        et = Ft[tet] @ b[:-1] + b[-1]\n324\t        prior = math.log(ntr / ncr)\n325\t        # held-out log-likelihood of the full model vs the intercept-only (prior) model\n326\t        ll_full += float(np.sum(-np.logaddexp(0.0, ec + prior)) + np.sum(-np.logaddexp(0.0, -(et + prior))))\n327\t        ll_null += float(np.sum(-np.logaddexp(0.0, prior * np.ones(len(ec))))\n328\t                         + np.sum(-np.logaddexp(0.0, -prior * np.ones(len(et)))))\n329\t        mu = float(np.mean(ec))\n330\t        zc[tec] = ec - mu\n331\t        zt[tet] = et - mu\n332\t    lr = 2.0 * (ll_full - ll_null)\n333\t    return _positive_part_shrink(lr, float(d)), zc, zt\n334\t\n335\t\n336\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- weighted Mondrian thresholds\n337\tdef _row_threshold(s_sorted, cum, w_test, level_alpha):\n338\t    \"\"\"Per-test-row weighted conformal threshold; the row's own mass ``w_test`` sits at +inf.\"\"\"\n339\t    n = len(s_sorted)\n340\t    m = len(w_test)\n341\t    if n == 0:\n342\t        return np.full(m, math.inf)\n343\t    target = (1.0 - level_alpha - 1e-12) * (cum[-1] + w_test)\n344\t    idx = np.searchsorted(cum, target, side=\"left\")\n345\t    return np.where(idx >= n, math.inf, s_sorted[np.minimum(idx, n - 1)])\n346\t\n347\t\n348\tdef _weighted_group_thresholds(scores, weights, groups, n_groups, w_test, alpha, n_total_test=None,\n349\t                               z_group=_Z_GROUP, z_global=_Z_GLOBAL, n0=_SHRINK_N0):\n350\t    \"\"\"Weighted Mondrian thresholds, one per (test row, group): array of shape [n_test, n_groups].\n351\t\n352\t    Calibration rows carry density-ratio weights; each test row carries its own weight at +inf.\n353\t    Margins use the effective sample size n_eff = (sum w)^2 / sum w^2 in place of the count (they\n354\t    reduce to the unweighted margins for unit weights); groups that cannot support a finite\n355\t    quantile fall back to the pooled weighted threshold and the rest are shrunk toward it.\n356\t    \"\"\"\n357\t    scores = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float64)\n358\t    weights = np.asarray(weights, dtype=np.float64)\n359\t    groups = np.asarray(groups)\n360\t    w_test = np.asarray(w_test, dtype=np.float64)\n361\t    m = len(w_test)\n362\t    a = float(alpha)\n363\t    var = a * (1.0 - a)\n364\t    inv_m = 0.0 if not n_total_test else 1.0 / float(n_total_test)\n365\t\n366\t    order = np.argsort(scores, kind=\"stable\")\n367\t    s_all, w_all = scores[order], weights[order]\n368\t    cum_all = np.cumsum(w_all)\n369\t    n_eff_all = cum_all[-1] ** 2 / np.sum(w_all ** 2)\n370\t    a_glob = max(a - z_global * math.sqrt(var * (1.0 / max(n_eff_all, 1.0) + inv_m)), 1e-6)\n371\t    q_glob = _row_threshold(s_all, cum_all, w_test, a_glob)\n372\t    q_glob = np.where(np.isfinite(q_glob), q_glob, _row_threshold(s_all, cum_all, w_test, a))\n373\t\n374\t    q = np.repeat(q_glob[:, None], n_groups, axis=1)\n375\t    for g in range(n_groups):\n376\t        sel = groups == g\n377\t        if not np.any(sel):\n378\t            continue\n379\t        og = np.argsort(scores[sel], kind=\"stable\")\n380\t        sg, wg = scores[sel][og], weights[sel][og]\n381\t        cum = np.cumsum(wg)\n382\t        n_eff = cum[-1] ** 2 / np.sum(wg ** 2)\n383\t        finite_a = np.isfinite(_row_threshold(sg, cum, w_test, a))\n384\t        k_g = float(n_groups) * inv_m\n385\t        a_g = max(a - z_group * math.sqrt(var * (1.0 / max(n_eff, 1.0) + k_g)), 1e-6)\n386\t        tg = _row_threshold(sg, cum, w_test, a_g)\n387\t        tg = np.where(np.isfinite(tg), tg, sg[-1])\n388\t        lam = n_eff / (n_eff + n0)\n389\t        q[:, g] = np.where(finite_a, lam * tg + (1.0 - lam) * q_glob, q_glob)\n390\t    return q\n391\t\n392\t\n393\tdef _finalize(request):\n394\t    probs = np.concatenate(_state[\"probs\"], axis=0)\n395\t    labels = np.concatenate(_state[\"labels\"], axis=0)\n396\t    N, K = probs.shape\n397\t    alpha = float(request[\"alpha\"])\n398\t    M = int(request.get(\"n_test\", 0)) or None\n399\t    scores = _score_matrix(probs)[np.arange(N), labels]\n400\t    _state[\"K\"] = K\n401\t    _state[\"alpha\"] = alpha\n402\t    _state[\"M\"] = M\n403\t    _state[\"cal_scores\"] = scores\n404\t    if K <= _MAX_CLASSCOND_K:\n405\t        _state[\"mode\"] = \"class\"\n406\t        _state[\"n_groups\"] = K\n407\t        _state[\"cal_groups\"] = labels\n408\t        _state[\"q\"] = mondrian_conformal_quantile(scores, labels, K, alpha, M)\n409\t    else:\n410\t        n_bins = int(min(_MAX_BINS, max(1, N // _MIN_BIN)))\n411\t        maxp = probs.max(axis=1)\n412\t        edges = _bin_edges(maxp, n_bins)\n413\t        bins = np.searchsorted(edges, maxp, side=\"right\")\n414\t        _state[\"mode\"] = \"bin\"\n415\t        _state[\"edges\"] = edges\n416\t        _state[\"n_groups\"] = n_bins\n417\t        _state[\"cal_groups\"] = bins\n418\t        _state[\"q\"] = mondrian_conformal_quantile(scores, bins, n_bins, alpha, M)\n419\t    # calibration summary features for the domain classifier (standardised with calibration moments)\n420\t    try:\n421\t        F = _summary_features(probs)\n422\t        mu = F.mean(axis=0)\n423\t        sd = F.std(axis=0)\n424\t        sd = np.where(sd > 1e-8, sd, 1.0)\n425\t        _state[\"F_mu\"], _state[\"F_sd\"] = mu, sd\n426\t        _state[\"F_cal\"] = np.clip((F - mu) / sd, -_FEAT_CLIP, _FEAT_CLIP)\n427\t        _state[\"fold_cal\"] = _state[\"rng\"].permutation(N) % 2\n428\t        _state[\"F_test\"] = []\n429\t    except Exception:  # pragma: no cover - keep the unweighted path usable\n430\t        _state[\"F_cal\"] = None\n431\t\n432\t\n433\tdef _unweighted_mask(probs, sc):\n434\t    q = _state[\"q\"]\n435\t    if _state[\"mode\"] == \"class\":\n436\t        return sc <= q[None, :]\n437\t    b = np.searchsorted(_state[\"edges\"], probs.max(axis=1), side=\"right\")\n438\t    return sc <= q[b][:, None]\n439\t\n440\t\n441\tdef _weighted_mask(probs, sc):\n442\t    \"\"\"Weighted mask for the current chunk, or None if no shift is detected / anything fails.\"\"\"\n443\t    if _state.get(\"F_cal\") is None:\n444\t        return None\n445\t    Fn = np.clip((_summary_features(probs) - _state[\"F_mu\"]) / _state[\"F_sd\"], -_FEAT_CLIP, _FEAT_CLIP)\n446\t    _state[\"F_test\"].append(Fn)\n447\t    Ft = np.concatenate(_state[\"F_test\"], axis=0)\n448\t    if Ft.shape[0] < _MIN_TEST_DOMAIN or not np.all(np.isfinite(Ft)):\n449\t        return None\n450\t    beta, zc, zt = _domain_logweights(_state[\"F_cal\"], Ft, _state[\"fold_cal\"])\n451\t    if not np.isfinite(beta) or beta <= _BETA_ON:\n452\t        return None\n453\t    lim = math.log(_W_CLIP)\n454\t    w_cal = np.exp(np.clip(beta * zc, -lim, lim))\n455\t    w_t = np.exp(np.clip(beta * zt[-len(probs):], -lim, lim))\n456\t    if not (np.all(np.isfinite(w_cal)) and np.all(np.isfinite(w_t))):\n457\t        return None\n458\t    q = _weighted_group_thresholds(_state[\"cal_scores\"], w_cal, _state[\"cal_groups\"], _state[\"n_groups\"],\n459\t                                   w_t, _state[\"alpha\"], _state[\"M\"])\n460\t    if np.any(np.isnan(q)):\n461\t        return None\n462\t    if _state[\"mode\"] == \"class\":\n463\t        return sc <= q\n464\t    b = np.searchsorted(_state[\"edges\"], probs.max(axis=1), side=\"right\")\n465\t    return sc <= q[np.arange(len(probs)), b][:, None]\n466\t\n467\t\n468\tdef handle(request):\n469\t    op = request[\"op\"]\n470\t    if op == \"reset\":\n471\t        _state.clear()\n472\t        _state[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(int(request[\"seed\"]))\n473\t        _state[\"probs\"] = []\n474\t        _state[\"labels\"] = []\n475\t        return {\"ok\": True}\n476\t    if op == \"calibrate\":\n477\t        _state[\"probs\"].append(_decode(request[\"probs\"]).astype(np.float64))\n478\t        _state[\"labels\"].append(_decode(request[\"labels\"]).astype(np.int64))\n479\t        if request[\"chunk_index\"] == request[\"num_chunks\"] - 1:\n480\t            _finalize(request)\n481\t        return {\"ok\": True}\n482\t    if op == \"predict\":\n483\t        probs = _decode(request[\"probs\"]).astype(np.float64)\n484\t        sc = _score_matrix(probs)\n485\t        mask = None\n486\t        try:\n487\t            mask = _weighted_mask(probs, sc)\n488\t        except Exception:\n489\t            mask = None\n490\t        if mask is None:\n491\t            mask = _unweighted_mask(probs, sc)\n492\t        return {\"sets\": _encode_mask(mask)}\n493\t    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")\n494\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"163efe90-675b-4e09-a080-713d4bfbbf15","uuid":"a7870926-b267-4249-93c4-ef268be627ab","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:48:09.573Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/paper/results/ideas/02_gated_domain_classifier_weighted_mondrian_conformal/program_1/src/program.py","content":"\"\"\"Candidate conformal prediction-set procedure for compositional (softmax) outputs.\n\nEntry point: ``handle(request) -> response`` (``python_rpc_v1:handle``).  The wire protocol is\nidentical to the starter (reset / calibrate / predict; responses ``{\"ok\": true}`` and\n``{\"sets\": MASK}``); see the starter docstring for the message layout.  No diagnostic fields are\nadded to any response.\n\nMethod (simplex-geometry aware split conformal with Mondrian calibration):\n\n* Score: LAC score ``1 - p[label]`` (an Aitchison-vertex score is available as an alternative\n  through ``_SCORE`` but the LAC score gave the smallest sets in design, see notes in memory).\n* K <= 10: the evaluator's slices are classes, so we use class-conditional (Mondrian by label)\n  thresholds, shrunk toward the pooled threshold for classes with few calibration rows.\n* K > 10: Mondrian by predicted-confidence bin (max probability), a taxon that depends on x only\n  so the guarantee is exact conditional on the bin.\n* Finite-sample quantile level ``ceil((n + 1)(1 - alpha)) / n`` with a small variance-aware\n  inflation: the expected under-coverage penalty is far steeper than the size cost of a tiny\n  extra margin, and the margin scales with the Beta(n + 1 - l, l) coverage standard deviation.\n\nGated domain-classifier weighting (this candidate's addition): the unlabeled test probabilities\nseen so far are compared with the calibration probabilities through a cross-fitted, ridge-penalised\nlogistic domain classifier on a few sorted-probability summary features.  The held-out\nlikelihood-ratio statistic LR gives a positive-part shrinkage beta = max(0, 1 - d / LR); when\nbeta is (numerically) zero -- always the case under exchangeability, where the held-out LR is\nnon-positive -- the unweighted Mondrian thresholds above are used verbatim (exact no-op).  Otherwise\nper-test-row weighted Mondrian thresholds (Tibshirani et al. 2019, test mass at +inf) are used,\nwith effective-sample-size margins; any non-finite quantity falls back to the unweighted path.\n\nThe remaining helpers (CLR/ILR transforms, Aitchison distance, ILR volume, worst-slab coverage,\nweighted conformal quantile, Beta coverage law, paired sign-flip test, Holm correction) implement\nthe evaluation protocol of the research idea; they are only used internally.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport math\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ntry:  # scipy is optional for the serving path\n    import scipy.stats\nexcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover\n    scipy = None\n\n_state = {}\n\n_SCORE = \"lac\"          # \"lac\" or \"aitchison\"\n_EPS = 1e-6             # simplex floor for log-ratio transforms\n_Z_GLOBAL = 0.7         # margin multipliers (in coverage standard deviations)\n_Z_GROUP = 0.6\n_SHRINK_N0 = 20.0       # pseudo-count for shrinking group thresholds toward the pooled one\n_MIN_BIN = 80           # minimal calibration rows per confidence bin\n_MAX_BINS = 10\n_MAX_CLASSCOND_K = 10\n_RIDGE = 1.0            # ridge penalty of the domain classifier (standardised features)\n_MIN_TEST_DOMAIN = 40   # minimal unlabeled test rows before the domain classifier is fitted\n_BETA_ON = 1e-3         # weights are used only if the shrinkage factor exceeds this\n_W_CLIP = 8.0           # weights clipped to [1/_W_CLIP, _W_CLIP]\n_FEAT_CLIP = 8.0        # standardised features clipped to +-_FEAT_CLIP\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- wire helpers\ndef _decode(obj):\n    dtype = np.dtype(obj[\"dtype\"]).newbyteorder(\"<\")\n    arr = np.frombuffer(base64.b64decode(obj[\"data\"]), dtype=dtype)\n    return arr.reshape(obj[\"shape\"])\n\n\ndef _encode_mask(mask):\n    packed = np.packbits(mask.astype(np.uint8), axis=1)\n    return {\"dtype\": \"uint8\", \"shape\": [int(mask.shape[0]), int(mask.shape[1])],\n            \"encoding\": \"packbits_base64\", \"data\": base64.b64encode(packed.tobytes()).decode(\"ascii\")}\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- compositional geometry\ndef _close(p, eps=_EPS):\n    p = np.clip(np.asarray(p, dtype=np.float64), eps, None)\n    return p / p.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n\n\ndef clr_transform(p, eps=_EPS):\n    \"\"\"Centred log-ratio transform of compositions along the last axis (with simplex floor).\"\"\"\n    lp = np.log(_close(p, eps))\n    return lp - lp.mean(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n\n\ndef _helmert_basis(D):\n    \"\"\"Orthonormal basis (D x (D-1)) of the CLR hyperplane (Helmert contrast matrix).\"\"\"\n    V = np.zeros((D, D - 1))\n    for j in range(1, D):\n        V[:j, j - 1] = 1.0 / j\n        V[j, j - 1] = -1.0\n        V[:, j - 1] *= math.sqrt(j / (j + 1.0))\n    return V\n\n\ndef ilr_transform(p, eps=_EPS):\n    \"\"\"Isometric log-ratio coordinates in R^(D-1) (Egozcue et al. style Helmert basis).\"\"\"\n    c = clr_transform(p, eps)\n    return c @ _helmert_basis(c.shape[-1])\n\n\ndef aitchison_distance(a, b, eps=_EPS):\n    \"\"\"Aitchison distance = Euclidean distance between CLR (equivalently ILR) coordinates.\"\"\"\n    return np.linalg.norm(clr_transform(a, eps) - clr_transform(b, eps), axis=-1)\n\n\ndef ilr_log_volume(radius, D):\n    \"\"\"Log-volume of a (D-1)-dimensional ILR-space ball: (D-1) log r + log V_{D-1}(1).\"\"\"\n    d = D - 1\n    return d * np.log(np.maximum(radius, 1e-300)) + (d / 2.0) * math.log(math.pi) - math.lgamma(d / 2.0 + 1.0)\n\n\ndef _score_matrix(probs):\n    \"\"\"Nonconformity score of every candidate label, shape [n, K].\"\"\"\n    if _SCORE == \"aitchison\":\n        K = probs.shape[1]\n        c = clr_transform(probs)\n        lo, hi = math.log(_EPS), math.log(1.0)\n        # smoothed vertex e_j has clr = log(v) - mean(log v)\n        v = np.full(K, _EPS)\n        out = np.empty_like(probs, dtype=np.float64)\n        for j in range(K):\n            vj = v.copy()\n            vj[j] = 1.0\n            vj = vj / vj.sum()\n            cj = np.log(vj) - np.log(vj).mean()\n            out[:, j] = np.linalg.norm(c - cj, axis=1)\n        return out\n    return 1.0 - probs\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- conformal quantiles\ndef finite_sample_level(n, alpha):\n    \"\"\"Conformal quantile level ceil((n + 1)(1 - alpha)) / n (may exceed 1 for tiny n).\"\"\"\n    alpha = float(alpha) + 1e-12  # guards float round-off in (n + 1) * (1 - alpha)\n    return np.ceil((n + 1) * (1 - alpha)) / n\n\n\ndef _kth_smallest(scores, level):\n    n = len(scores)\n    if n == 0 or level > 1.0:\n        return math.inf\n    k = int(np.rint(level * n))\n    return float(np.sort(scores)[min(max(k, 1), n) - 1])\n\n\ndef _quantile(scores, alpha):\n    scores = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float64)\n    return _kth_smallest(scores, finite_sample_level(len(scores), alpha))\n\n\ndef weighted_conformal_quantile(scores, weights, test_weight, alpha):\n    \"\"\"Likelihood-ratio weighted conformal quantile (Tibshirani et al. 2019).\n\n    Calibration points carry weights w(x_i); the test point's mass w(x) sits at +inf.\n    \"\"\"\n    scores = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float64)\n    weights = np.asarray(weights, dtype=np.float64)\n    order = np.argsort(scores)\n    s, w = scores[order], weights[order]\n    p = w / (w.sum() + test_weight)\n    cum = np.cumsum(p)\n    idx = np.searchsorted(cum, 1.0 - alpha - 1e-12, side=\"left\")\n    return math.inf if idx >= len(s) else float(s[idx])\n\n\ndef beta_coverage_law(n, alpha):\n    \"\"\"Frozen Beta(n + 1 - l, l) law of split-conformal coverage, l = floor((n + 1) alpha).\"\"\"\n    l = int(math.floor((n + 1) * alpha + 1e-12))\n    l = max(l, 1)\n    if scipy is not None:\n        return scipy.stats.beta(n + 1 - l, l)\n    return None\n\n\ndef mondrian_conformal_quantile(scores, groups, n_groups, alpha, n_total_test=None,\n                                z_group=_Z_GROUP, z_global=_Z_GLOBAL, n0=_SHRINK_N0):\n    \"\"\"Per-group conformal thresholds (Mondrian calibration) with pooled-threshold shrinkage.\n\n    ``scores`` are calibration scores, ``groups`` integer taxon ids in [0, n_groups).  Returns an\n    array ``q`` of length ``n_groups``.  Each group's level is the finite-sample level\n    ceil((n_g + 1)(1 - alpha_g))/n_g with alpha_g reduced by ``z_group`` coverage standard\n    deviations; groups too small to support a finite quantile fall back to the pooled threshold.\n    \"\"\"\n    scores = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float64)\n    groups = np.asarray(groups)\n    N = len(scores)\n    a = float(alpha)\n    var = a * (1.0 - a)\n    inv_m = 0.0 if not n_total_test else 1.0 / float(n_total_test)\n    a_glob = max(a - z_global * math.sqrt(var * (1.0 / max(N, 1) + inv_m)), 1e-6)\n    q_glob = _quantile(scores, a_glob)\n    if not np.isfinite(q_glob):\n        q_glob = _quantile(scores, a)\n    q = np.full(n_groups, q_glob)\n    for g in range(n_groups):\n        sg = scores[groups == g]\n        ng = len(sg)\n        if ng == 0 or not np.isfinite(_quantile(sg, a)):\n            continue\n        k_g = float(n_groups) * inv_m if n_total_test else 0.0\n        a_g = max(a - z_group * math.sqrt(var * (1.0 / ng + k_g)), 1e-6)\n        qg = _kth_smallest(sg, min(1.0, finite_sample_level(ng, a_g)))\n        lam = ng / (ng + n0)\n        q[g] = lam * qg + (1.0 - lam) * q_glob\n    return q\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- evaluation helpers\ndef worst_slab_coverage(covered, slab_ids):\n    \"\"\"Minimum empirical coverage over slabs and the worst-slab gap to the best slab-free mean.\"\"\"\n    covered = np.asarray(covered, dtype=np.float64)\n    slab_ids = np.asarray(slab_ids)\n    covs = [covered[slab_ids == s].mean() for s in np.unique(slab_ids)]\n    return float(min(covs)) if covs else float(\"nan\")\n\n\ndef paired_sign_flip_test(diffs, n_perm=2000, seed=0):\n    \"\"\"Two-sided paired sign-flip permutation test on per-draw differences between methods.\"\"\"\n    diffs = np.asarray(diffs, dtype=np.float64)\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    obs = abs(diffs.mean())\n    signs = rng.choice([-1.0, 1.0], size=(n_perm, len(diffs)))\n    perm = np.abs((signs * diffs).mean(axis=1))\n    return float((1 + np.sum(perm >= obs - 1e-15)) / (n_perm + 1))\n\n\ndef holm_correction(pvals):\n    \"\"\"Holm-Bonferroni step-down adjusted p-values.\"\"\"\n    p = np.asarray(pvals, dtype=np.float64)\n    m = len(p)\n    order = np.argsort(p)\n    adj = np.empty(m)\n    running = 0.0\n    for rank, i in enumerate(order):\n        running = max(running, (m - rank) * p[i])\n        adj[i] = min(1.0, running)\n    return adj\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- serving path\ndef _bin_edges(maxp, n_bins):\n    if n_bins <= 1:\n        return np.zeros(0)\n    return np.quantile(maxp, np.arange(1, n_bins) / n_bins)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- domain-classifier weights\ndef _summary_features(probs):\n    \"\"\"Low-dimensional sorted-probability summary of each row, shape [n, 5].\n\n    [logit(max prob), top1-top2 log ratio, normalised entropy, mean top-5 log prob minus top-1\n    log prob, log of the normalised Gini impurity]; all from probabilities clipped at 1e-6.\n    \"\"\"\n    p = np.clip(np.asarray(probs, dtype=np.float64), _EPS, 1.0)\n    K = p.shape[1]\n    ps = -np.sort(-p, axis=1)\n    ls = np.log(ps)\n    k5 = min(K, 5)\n    pmax = ps[:, 0]\n    f1 = np.log(pmax) - np.log(np.maximum(1.0 - pmax, _EPS))\n    f2 = ls[:, 0] - ls[:, 1] if K > 1 else np.zeros(len(p))\n    f3 = -(p * np.log(p)).sum(axis=1) / max(math.log(K), 1e-12)\n    f4 = ls[:, :k5].mean(axis=1) - ls[:, 0]\n    gini = (1.0 - (p * p).sum(axis=1)) / max(1.0 - 1.0 / K, 1e-12)\n    f5 = np.log(np.clip(gini, _EPS, None))\n    return np.stack([f1, f2, f3, f4, f5], axis=1)\n\n\ndef _fit_domain_logistic(X, y, sw, ridge=_RIDGE, iters=25):\n    \"\"\"Ridge-penalised weighted logistic regression by IRLS (Newton); returns [coef..., intercept].\"\"\"\n    n, d = X.shape\n    A = np.concatenate([X, np.ones((n, 1))], axis=1)\n    R = ridge * np.eye(d + 1)\n    R[d, d] = 1e-8\n    b = np.zeros(d + 1)\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        eta = np.clip(A @ b, -30.0, 30.0)\n        p = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-eta))\n        g = A.T @ (sw * (p - y)) + R @ b\n        H = (A * (sw * p * (1.0 - p))[:, None]).T @ A + R\n        step = np.linalg.solve(H, g)\n        step = np.clip(step, -5.0, 5.0)\n        b = b - step\n        if np.max(np.abs(step)) < 1e-7:\n            break\n    return b\n\n\ndef _positive_part_shrink(lr, df):\n    \"\"\"James-Stein style positive-part shrinkage factor beta = max(0, 1 - df / LR).\"\"\"\n    if not np.isfinite(lr) or lr <= 0.0:\n        return 0.0\n    return max(0.0, 1.0 - df / lr)\n\n\ndef _domain_logweights(Fc, Ft, fold_c):\n    \"\"\"Cross-fitted domain-classifier log density ratios (test over calibration).\n\n    Returns (beta, z_cal, z_test): ``beta`` the positive-part shrinkage factor computed from the\n    held-out likelihood-ratio statistic, ``z`` the centred held-out log-odds (balanced classes).\n    A row's value always comes from a model fitted on the other fold (2-fold cross-fitting over\n    calibration rows and over test rows).\n    \"\"\"\n    nc, d = Fc.shape\n    nt = Ft.shape[0]\n    fold_t = np.arange(nt) % 2\n    zc = np.zeros(nc)\n    zt = np.zeros(nt)\n    ll_full = 0.0\n    ll_null = 0.0\n    for f in (0, 1):\n        trc, tec = fold_c != f, fold_c == f\n        trt, tet = fold_t != f, fold_t == f\n        ncr, ntr = int(trc.sum()), int(trt.sum())\n        if ncr < 5 or ntr < 5 or tec.sum() < 1 or tet.sum() < 1:\n            return 0.0, zc, zt\n        X = np.concatenate([Fc[trc], Ft[trt]], axis=0)\n        y = np.concatenate([np.zeros(ncr), np.ones(ntr)])\n        n = ncr + ntr\n        sw = np.where(y > 0.5, n / (2.0 * ntr), n / (2.0 * ncr))\n        b = _fit_domain_logistic(X, y, sw)\n        ec = Fc[tec] @ b[:-1] + b[-1]\n        et = Ft[tet] @ b[:-1] + b[-1]\n        prior = math.log(ntr / ncr)\n        # held-out log-likelihood of the full model vs the intercept-only (prior) model\n        ll_full += float(np.sum(-np.logaddexp(0.0, ec + prior)) + np.sum(-np.logaddexp(0.0, -(et + prior))))\n        ll_null += float(np.sum(-np.logaddexp(0.0, prior * np.ones(len(ec))))\n                         + np.sum(-np.logaddexp(0.0, -prior * np.ones(len(et)))))\n        mu = float(np.mean(ec))\n        zc[tec] = ec - mu\n        zt[tet] = et - mu\n    lr = 2.0 * (ll_full - ll_null)\n    return _positive_part_shrink(lr, float(d)), zc, zt\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- weighted Mondrian thresholds\ndef _row_threshold(s_sorted, cum, w_test, level_alpha):\n    \"\"\"Per-test-row weighted conformal threshold; the row's own mass ``w_test`` sits at +inf.\"\"\"\n    n = len(s_sorted)\n    m = len(w_test)\n    if n == 0:\n        return np.full(m, math.inf)\n    target = (1.0 - level_alpha - 1e-12) * (cum[-1] + w_test)\n    idx = np.searchsorted(cum, target, side=\"left\")\n    return np.where(idx >= n, math.inf, s_sorted[np.minimum(idx, n - 1)])\n\n\ndef _weighted_group_thresholds(scores, weights, groups, n_groups, w_test, alpha, n_total_test=None,\n                               z_group=_Z_GROUP, z_global=_Z_GLOBAL, n0=_SHRINK_N0):\n    \"\"\"Weighted Mondrian thresholds, one per (test row, group): array of shape [n_test, n_groups].\n\n    Calibration rows carry density-ratio weights; each test row carries its own weight at +inf.\n    Margins use the effective sample size n_eff = (sum w)^2 / sum w^2 in place of the count (they\n    reduce to the unweighted margins for unit weights); groups that cannot support a finite\n    quantile fall back to the pooled weighted threshold and the rest are shrunk toward it.\n    \"\"\"\n    scores = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float64)\n    weights = np.asarray(weights, dtype=np.float64)\n    groups = np.asarray(groups)\n    w_test = np.asarray(w_test, dtype=np.float64)\n    m = len(w_test)\n    a = float(alpha)\n    var = a * (1.0 - a)\n    inv_m = 0.0 if not n_total_test else 1.0 / float(n_total_test)\n\n    order = np.argsort(scores, kind=\"stable\")\n    s_all, w_all = scores[order], weights[order]\n    cum_all = np.cumsum(w_all)\n    n_eff_all = cum_all[-1] ** 2 / np.sum(w_all ** 2)\n    a_glob = max(a - z_global * math.sqrt(var * (1.0 / max(n_eff_all, 1.0) + inv_m)), 1e-6)\n    q_glob = _row_threshold(s_all, cum_all, w_test, a_glob)\n    q_glob = np.where(np.isfinite(q_glob), q_glob, _row_threshold(s_all, cum_all, w_test, a))\n\n    q = np.repeat(q_glob[:, None], n_groups, axis=1)\n    for g in range(n_groups):\n        sel = groups == g\n        if not np.any(sel):\n            continue\n        og = np.argsort(scores[sel], kind=\"stable\")\n        sg, wg = scores[sel][og], weights[sel][og]\n        cum = np.cumsum(wg)\n        n_eff = cum[-1] ** 2 / np.sum(wg ** 2)\n        finite_a = np.isfinite(_row_threshold(sg, cum, w_test, a))\n        k_g = float(n_groups) * inv_m\n        a_g = max(a - z_group * math.sqrt(var * (1.0 / max(n_eff, 1.0) + k_g)), 1e-6)\n        tg = _row_threshold(sg, cum, w_test, a_g)\n        tg = np.where(np.isfinite(tg), tg, sg[-1])\n        lam = n_eff / (n_eff + n0)\n        q[:, g] = np.where(finite_a, lam * tg + (1.0 - lam) * q_glob, q_glob)\n    return q\n\n\ndef _finalize(request):\n    probs = np.concatenate(_state[\"probs\"], axis=0)\n    labels = np.concatenate(_state[\"labels\"], axis=0)\n    N, K = probs.shape\n    alpha = float(request[\"alpha\"])\n    M = int(request.get(\"n_test\", 0)) or None\n    scores = _score_matrix(probs)[np.arange(N), labels]\n    _state[\"K\"] = K\n    _state[\"alpha\"] = alpha\n    _state[\"M\"] = M\n    _state[\"cal_scores\"] = scores\n    if K <= _MAX_CLASSCOND_K:\n        _state[\"mode\"] = \"class\"\n        _state[\"n_groups\"] = K\n        _state[\"cal_groups\"] = labels\n        _state[\"q\"] = mondrian_conformal_quantile(scores, labels, K, alpha, M)\n    else:\n        n_bins = int(min(_MAX_BINS, max(1, N // _MIN_BIN)))\n        maxp = probs.max(axis=1)\n        edges = _bin_edges(maxp, n_bins)\n        bins = np.searchsorted(edges, maxp, side=\"right\")\n        _state[\"mode\"] = \"bin\"\n        _state[\"edges\"] = edges\n        _state[\"n_groups\"] = n_bins\n        _state[\"cal_groups\"] = bins\n        _state[\"q\"] = mondrian_conformal_quantile(scores, bins, n_bins, alpha, M)\n    # calibration summary features for the domain classifier (standardised with calibration moments)\n    try:\n        F = _summary_features(probs)\n        mu = F.mean(axis=0)\n        sd = F.std(axis=0)\n        sd = np.where(sd > 1e-8, sd, 1.0)\n        _state[\"F_mu\"], _state[\"F_sd\"] = mu, sd\n        _state[\"F_cal\"] = np.clip((F - mu) / sd, -_FEAT_CLIP, _FEAT_CLIP)\n        _state[\"fold_cal\"] = _state[\"rng\"].permutation(N) % 2\n        _state[\"F_test\"] = []\n    except Exception:  # pragma: no cover - keep the unweighted path usable\n        _state[\"F_cal\"] = None\n\n\ndef _unweighted_mask(probs, sc):\n    q = _state[\"q\"]\n    if _state[\"mode\"] == \"class\":\n        return sc <= q[None, :]\n    b = np.searchsorted(_state[\"edges\"], probs.max(axis=1), side=\"right\")\n    return sc <= q[b][:, None]\n\n\ndef _weighted_mask(probs, sc):\n    \"\"\"Weighted mask for the current chunk, or None if no shift is detected / anything fails.\"\"\"\n    if _state.get(\"F_cal\") is None:\n        return None\n    Fn = np.clip((_summary_features(probs) - _state[\"F_mu\"]) / _state[\"F_sd\"], -_FEAT_CLIP, _FEAT_CLIP)\n    _state[\"F_test\"].append(Fn)\n    Ft = np.concatenate(_state[\"F_test\"], axis=0)\n    if Ft.shape[0] < _MIN_TEST_DOMAIN or not np.all(np.isfinite(Ft)):\n        return None\n    beta, zc, zt = _domain_logweights(_state[\"F_cal\"], Ft, _state[\"fold_cal\"])\n    if not np.isfinite(beta) or beta <= _BETA_ON:\n        return None\n    lim = math.log(_W_CLIP)\n    w_cal = np.exp(np.clip(beta * zc, -lim, lim))\n    w_t = np.exp(np.clip(beta * zt[-len(probs):], -lim, lim))\n    if not (np.all(np.isfinite(w_cal)) and np.all(np.isfinite(w_t))):\n        return None\n    q = _weighted_group_thresholds(_state[\"cal_scores\"], w_cal, _state[\"cal_groups\"], _state[\"n_groups\"],\n                                   w_t, _state[\"alpha\"], _state[\"M\"])\n    if np.any(np.isnan(q)):\n        return None\n    if _state[\"mode\"] == \"class\":\n        return sc <= q\n    b = np.searchsorted(_state[\"edges\"], probs.max(axis=1), side=\"right\")\n    return sc <= q[np.arange(len(probs)), b][:, None]\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    op = request[\"op\"]\n    if op == \"reset\":\n        _state.clear()\n        _state[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(int(request[\"seed\"]))\n        _state[\"probs\"] = []\n        _state[\"labels\"] = []\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if op == \"calibrate\":\n        _state[\"probs\"].append(_decode(request[\"probs\"]).astype(np.float64))\n        _state[\"labels\"].append(_decode(request[\"labels\"]).astype(np.int64))\n        if request[\"chunk_index\"] == request[\"num_chunks\"] - 1:\n            _finalize(request)\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if op == \"predict\":\n        probs = _decode(request[\"probs\"]).astype(np.float64)\n        sc = _score_matrix(probs)\n        mask = None\n        try:\n            mask = _weighted_mask(probs, sc)\n        except Exception:\n            mask = None\n        if mask is None:\n            mask = _unweighted_mask(probs, sc)\n        return {\"sets\": _encode_mask(mask)}\n    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")\n","numLines":494,"startLine":1,"totalLines":494}}}
