{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pu6feS1Ai68sRXZSfiAWpp","type":"tool_result","content":"25\nCina2026QuantifyingCC | Scientific Reports | Andrea Cina and Maria Monzon and Fabio Galbusera a 2026\nBethell2023RobustUQ | AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence | Daniel Bethell and Simos Gerasimou and R. Calinesc 2023\nFillioux2024AreFM | Trans. Mach. Learn. Res. | Leo Fillioux and Julio Silva-Rodr'iguez and I. Ben 2024\nMelki2023GroupConditionalCP | 2023 IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision Workshops (ICCVW) | P. Melki and L. Bombrun and Boubacar Diallo and Jé 2023\nXu2022ConformalPS | arXiv.org | Chen Xu and Yao Xie 2022\nLiu2024CAdapterAD | European Conference on Artificial Intelligence | Kangdao Liu and Hao Zeng and Jianguo Huang and Hui 2024\nRueda2007ProgressIP | Iberoamerican Congress on Pattern Recognition | Luis Rueda and Domingo Mery and Josef Kittler 2007\nGelvez2025ConformalPF | 2025 XXV Symposium of Image, Signal Processing, and Artificial Vision (STSIVA) | Santiago Gelvez and D. Clavijo and David Romo-Buch 2025\nGibbs2023ConformalPW | Journal of The Royal Statistical Society Series B-statistical Methodology | Isaac Gibbs and John J. Cherian and E. Candès 2023\nDing2023ClassConditionalCP | Neural Information Processing Systems | Tiffany Ding and Anastasios Nikolas Angelopoulos a 2023\nKiyani2024LengthOI | Neural Information Processing Systems | Shayan Kiyani and George Pappas and H. Hassani 2024\nLöfström2015BiasRT | Intelligent Data Analysis | Tuwe Löfström and Henrik Boström and H. Linusson a 2015\nShi2024ConformalPF | Neural Information Processing Systems | Yuan-Jie Shi and Subhankar Ghosh and Taha Belkhouj 2024\nJin2024ConfidenceOT | Confidence on the Focal: Conformal Prediction with Selection-Conditional Coverage | Ying Jin and Zhi-Mei Ren 2024\nDabah2024OnTS | International Conference on Machine Learning | Lahav Dabah and Tom Tirer 2024\nBairaktari2025KandinskyCP | International Conference on Machine Learning | Konstantina Bairaktari and Jia-Yun Wu and Steven Z 2025\nDing2025ConformalPF | International Conference on Learning Representations | Tiffany Ding and Jean-Baptiste Fermanian and Josep 2025\nO'Sullivan2025BridgingCP | IEEE Conference on Decision and Control | Niall O'Sullivan and Licio Romao and Kostas Margel 2025\nKaur2025ConformalPS | arXiv.org | J. Kaur and Michael I. Jordan and Ahmed M. Alaa 2025\nHuang2024CONFINECP | arXiv.org | Linhui Huang and S. Lala and N. Jha 2024\nDewolf2023ConditionalVO | Conditional validity of heteroskedastic conformal regression | Nicolas Dewolf and B. de Baets and W. Waegeman 2023\nBraun2025MultivariateSR | Multivariate Standardized Residuals for Conformal Prediction | Sacha Braun and E. Berta and Michael I. Jordan and 2025\nLöfström2022TutorialFU | International Symposium on Conformal and Probabilistic Prediction with Applications | Tuwe Löfström and A. Ryasik and U. Johansson 2022\nJavanmardi2025OptimalCP | arXiv.org | A. Javanmardi and Soroush H. Zargarbashi and Santo 2025\nChakraborty2024DistributionfreeCP | International Symposium on Conformal and Probabilistic Prediction with Applications | S. Chakraborty and Chhavi Tyagi and Haiyan Qiao an 2024\n---\nname: validate-paper\ndescription: Validate grounded paper artifacts and compile LaTeX PDF with strict fail-fast checks.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nRun final quality gate for the generated paper.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- After `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, and `claims_grounding.json` are written.\n- Before declaring final paper success.\n\n# What to do\n1. Validate sections and citation keys:\n```bash\npython scripts/validate_tex_refs.py \\\n  --tex paper.tex \\\n  --bib references.bib\n```\nRequire a substantive embedded Supplementary Information section after the bibliography. It must\nuse `\\\\appendix` and `\\\\section{Supplementary Information}`, contain grounded visible content plus\nat least one subsection, table, or figure, and contain no template placeholder text.\n2. Validate claim mappings, bibliography/provenance consistency, and every `@evidence[[...]]` link in the `scientific-evidence/` bundle:\n```bash\npython ../write-paper/scripts/validate_claims.py \\\n  --paper-data paper_data.json \\\n  --references references_provenance.json \\\n  --bib references.bib \\\n  --claims claims_grounding.json \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\nThis delegates to the `scientific-evidence` skill verifier, which classifies every `@evidence[[...]]` link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`. Any `dangling` link (or an `@evidence[[...]]` token with no `scientific-evidence/` bundle present) is a hard error and must be sent back to the paper-writing agent for repair.\n3. Validate figure manifest and figure readability budget when `figure_manifest.json` is present or `paper_strategy.json` requires figures. The canonical schema is `templates/figure_manifest.schema.json`.\n```bash\npython .claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\n4. Compile:\n```bash\nbash scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n```\nThe compile script also validates that Supplementary Information is visibly rendered on a page\nafter References with substantive content. Source-only structure checks are not sufficient for\nconditional or literal LaTeX constructs.\nIt records and validates every LaTeX input, restricts BibTeX to the canonical `references.bib`,\nand removes inherited Kpathsea path overrides before compiling.\n5. Require `paper.pdf` to exist.\n6. When `paper_data.json.paper_profile == \"standalone\"`, also fail on visible paper language that leaks pipeline terms such as `eligible`, `correct and eligible`, `correctness rate`, `worker_01`, `worker_02`, `combined_score`, or similar internal wording.\n7. When the selected format or venue guidance requires real author metadata, also fail on anonymous or generic placeholder author blocks and emit soft warnings when title/abstract/introduction/conclusion lack venue-r