{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvwVopwKDnm6A9UsTRAA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012JVZaF6dAGaSDSxC3haQE2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'; t=open(p).read()\na=\"Since exchangeable-case gaps are small, the marginal term is plausibly dominated by shifted cases, but we cannot establish this without per-case results. The largest single residual cost is therefore marginal under-coverage, not set size. We do not attribute the residual shift or slice gaps to statistical noise, to the density-ratio estimation, or to a validity failure of the weighting: no gate-level diagnostics are retained.\"\nassert a in t\nb=a+\"\"\"\n\n\\\\begin{figure}[t]\n\\\\centering\n\\\\includegraphics[width=0.9\\\\textwidth]{figures/loss_decomposition.pdf}\n\\\\caption{Decomposition of the sealed final mean loss of the studied procedure into the three terms of Eq.~\\\\eqref{eq:loss}. The set-size and worst-slice terms are computed from the retained metrics; the marginal term is the remainder. The best baseline's total loss is shown without decomposition because its components are not retained.}\n\\\\label{fig:decomp}\n\\\\end{figure}\"\"\"\nt=t.replace(a,b)\na2=\"\\\\paragraph{Practical reading.}\"\ntab=\"\"\"\\\\paragraph{Evidence inventory.} Table~\\\\ref{tab:inventory} summarises which quantities that a reader might want are available and which are unknown, so that gaps in the evidence are not mistaken for null results.\n\n\\\\begin{table}[t]\n\\\\centering\n\\\\caption{Evidence inventory for the sealed final evaluation.}\n\\\\label{tab:inventory}\n\\\\begin{tabular}{p{0.46\\\\textwidth}p{0.42\\\\textwidth}}\n\\\\toprule\nAvailable & Not retained (unknown) \\\\\\\\\n\\\\midrule\nAggregate score, best-baseline aggregate score, paired margin and bootstrap interval & Identity and individual scores of the four baselines \\\\\\\\\nFive per-seed scores; failed-episode count; control pass fraction & Per-case and per-family results; which cases drive shift and slice gaps \\\\\\\\\nExchangeable, shift, worst-slice and size-ratio aggregates & $\\\\alpha$, $K$ and sample sizes of the sealed cases \\\\\\\\\nSource of the studied procedure and of the evaluator code & Gate-activation frequency; cause of the development-to-final drop; cause of the V3--V2 tie \\\\\\\\\n\\\\bottomrule\n\\\\end{tabular}\n\\\\end{table}\n\n\"\"\"\nt=t.replace(a2,tab+a2,1)\na3=\"reporting only average coverage and size would not have revealed the residual shift and slice gaps seen here.\"\nassert a3 in t\nt=t.replace(a3,a3+\" A stronger study built on the same protocol would additionally report per-baseline and per-case scores, a within-case ablation that separates the Mondrian grouping, the gate and the weighting, activation logs for the gate, and at least one evaluation on classifier outputs from a natural dataset. Because the composite score is a fixed weighting of three components, we also recommend reporting the three components separately for every method, as the decomposition in Figure~\\\\ref{fig:decomp} shows that the headline number can hide where the remaining loss sits.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nE\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1; bibtex paper >/dev/null 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex 2>&1 | grep -E \"^!|Output written|undefined\"\nPYTHONPATH=/agent-tmp/pylib python3 - 2>/dev/null <<'E'\nimport pymupdf\nd=pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\nfor i,p in enumerate(d):\n    t=[l for l in p.get_text().split('\\n') if l.strip()]\n    bl=[b for b in p.get_text('blocks') if b[3]<720 and b[1]>60]\n    print(i+1, round(max(b[3] for b in bl)) if bl else 0, t[-3][:60])\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2226,"cache_read_input_tokens":188513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2226},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"163efe90-675b-4e09-a080-713d4bfbbf15","uuid":"cb3ad0ae-1037-45fb-9cbe-0a99b3d681de","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:56:13.310Z","request_id":"req_011CgvwVkrMKXqUCwXGHEWy6"}
