{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvwXQ12P5m95CNmgeNRQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WF42fiV3KZge8zmSzGF1xB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'; t=open(p).read()\na=\"\\\\paragraph{Weighted calibration under covariate shift.}\"\nprop=\"\"\"\\\\paragraph{Proposition (Mondrian coverage; textbook).}\nLet $G$ be a partition cell function of $(x,y)$ and let the calibration scores of cell $g$ be $s_1,\\\\dots,s_{n_g}$, exchangeable with the test score $s_{\\\\mathrm{new}}$ conditional on the test point lying in cell $g$, with no ties. Take $q_g$ equal to the $k_g$-th smallest calibration score, $k_g=\\\\lceil(n_g+1)(1-\\\\alpha)\\\\rceil$. Then $\\\\Pr(s_{\\\\mathrm{new}}\\\\le q_g\\\\mid G=g)\\\\ge1-\\\\alpha$.\n\\\\emph{Proof sketch.} By exchangeability the rank of $s_{\\\\mathrm{new}}$ among the $n_g+1$ scores is uniform on $\\\\{1,\\\\dots,n_g+1\\\\}$. The event $s_{\\\\mathrm{new}}\\\\le q_g$ holds exactly when this rank is at most $k_g$, which has probability $k_g/(n_g+1)\\\\ge1-\\\\alpha$; ties only increase the probability. $\\\\square$\nFor $G=y$ the cell is observable only at calibration time, and the set $\\\\{k:1-p_k(x)\\\\le q_k\\\\}$ covers the true label $y$ with class-conditional probability at least $1-\\\\alpha$ because the event is $\\\\{s(x,y)\\\\le q_y\\\\}$. For $G$ a function of $x$ alone the cell is known at prediction time. The guarantee is conditional on the cell and does not extend to other partitions, such as the evaluator's slices when $K>10$ are not the Mondrian bins. The variance-aware margins used below lower $\\\\alpha_g$ and therefore only increase this probability. The data-dependent gate below is \\\\emph{not} covered by this argument: it uses unlabelled calibration and test features, it treats the two groups asymmetrically, and we have not derived a guarantee for the draws on which it activates under exchangeability. We therefore use the proposition only as background for the fallback branch.\n\n\"\"\"\nassert a in t\nt=t.replace(a,prop+a,1)\nb=\"\\\\subsection{Studied procedure}\"\nhyp=\"\"\"\\\\subsection{Design rationale and hypotheses}\nThe procedure is built around three expectations, each tied to one component. \\\\textbf{H1}: grouping calibration by label (small $K$) or confidence bin (large $K$) should shrink worst-slice under-coverage relative to pooled calibration, because it makes the coverage guarantee hold within the evaluator's slices when those coincide with the groups. \\\\textbf{H2}: a gated, cross-fitted density-ratio correction should reduce marginal under-coverage on shifted cases, while a gate that stays closed leaves exchangeable behaviour and the negative controls untouched. \\\\textbf{H3}: group-indicator quantile-regression thresholds could further reduce worst-slice gaps when the groups are overlapping. The retained evidence addresses these only partially: H1 is not isolated (no pooled-versus-Mondrian pair of otherwise identical configurations was retained, and baseline identities are unknown); H2 is addressed by the development comparison V1 versus V2 and by the sealed shift-case gap; H3 is untestable from V3 because V3 coincides with V2. The aim of the sealed evaluation is thus the narrower statement of Section~\\\\ref{sec:results} about the composite score, not a verification of each hypothesis.\n\n\"\"\"\nassert b in t\nt=t.replace(b,hyp+b,1)\nt=t.replace(\"\\\\section{Results}\",\"\\\\section{Results}\\\\label{sec:results}\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nE\ngrep -n \"such as the evaluator's slices when\" paper.tex | head -2"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1446,"cache_read_input_tokens":192667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1446},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"163efe90-675b-4e09-a080-713d4bfbbf15","uuid":"d34a5212-28d4-4d14-b905-651bbb301fe0","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:56:55.657Z","request_id":"req_011CgvwXMQzoquvzdMvadDjY"}
