{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvwbnwmHgmxPKEY5yWuM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PmCfWbDLUW4TkdVD7jEsTa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'; t=open(p).read()\na=\"Only the sealed numbers should be used for conclusions.\"\nassert a in t\ntab=a+\"\"\"\n\n\\\\begin{table}[t]\n\\\\centering\n\\\\caption{The selected procedure on development data (seeds 101--103) and on sealed final data (seeds 9001--9005). Different cases and seeds; shown side by side for transparency, not as a paired comparison.}\n\\\\label{tab:devfinal}\n\\\\begin{tabular}{lrr}\n\\\\toprule\nMetric & Development & Sealed final \\\\\\\\\n\\\\midrule\nComposite score & 0.9192 & 0.8416 \\\\\\\\\nExchangeable marginal gap & 0.0003 & 0.0017 \\\\\\\\\nWorst-slice gap & 0.0376 & 0.0675 \\\\\\\\\nShift-case marginal gap & 0.0201 & 0.0536 \\\\\\\\\nSet-size ratio & 0.181 & 0.209 \\\\\\\\\n\\\\bottomrule\n\\\\end{tabular}\n% @evidence[[derived/derived_stats.json#variants]] @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics]]\n\\\\end{table}\"\"\"\nt=t.replace(a,tab,1)\nb=\"\\\\paragraph{Practical reading.}\"\nthr=\"\"\"\\\\paragraph{Threats to validity.}\nThe synthetic generator is one parametric family (Gaussian logits with a true-class signal, heteroscedastic signal strength, a prior tilt and temperature), and the predictor's calibration is not varied independently; real softmax outputs may behave differently. For $K\\\\le10$ the evaluator's slices are classes, which are exactly the Mondrian groups of the studied procedure, so part of its advantage on the slice axis reflects a match between method and metric by design; the class-wise baseline shares this alignment, but its individual score is not retained. The development score was used to select the configuration, so development numbers are optimistic selection-biased proxies; the sealed evaluation was run once on disjoint data. Finally, the composite loss multiplies the marginal gap by $1/\\\\alpha$ and clips it, which makes the score insensitive to under-coverage beyond $\\\\alpha$ in a single case; the retained aggregates cannot show whether any case hit this clip.\n\n\"\"\"\nt=t.replace(b,thr+b,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nE\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1; bibtex paper >/dev/null 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex 2>&1 | grep -E \"^!|Output written|undefined\"\nPYTHONPATH=/agent-tmp/pylib python3 - 2>/dev/null <<'E'\nimport pymupdf\nd=pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\nfor i in range(7,10):\n    p=d[i]; ls=[l for l in p.get_text().split('\\n') if l.strip() and not l.strip().isdigit()]\n    bl=[b for b in p.get_text('blocks') if b[3]<720 and b[1]>60]\n    print(i+1, round(max(b[3] for b in bl)), ls[1][:50], '|', ls[-1][:50])\n    p.get_pixmap(dpi=50).save(f'/agent-tmp/z{i+1}.png')\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1339,"cache_read_input_tokens":200175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1339},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"163efe90-675b-4e09-a080-713d4bfbbf15","uuid":"81fa66ec-e218-46cb-8d31-d708a18d5d39","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:57:36.810Z","request_id":"req_011Cgvwbk4snBkzcLnPTMkGa"}
